<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15827" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-nŏto</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to mark out</i>, <i>note down</i> (not ante-Aug. and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meditabar aliquid enotabamque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 1, 6, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">figuras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6, 16, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verbum cui tribus litteris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 7, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signa nostra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 237</span></i>
			.—<b>Poet.</b>: pictis anas enotata
			pennis, Petr. poët. Sat. 93, 2, 4.</div>
